# Expected content delta between docs/agentic-harness.md (root handbook) and
# harness/core/.claude/skills/handoff-routing/agentic-harness.md (installed copy).
# Line-number-insensitive: check-sync's handbook-delta step compares `diff -U0 | grep ^[-+]`
# (headers stripped) against this file. When one of these lines legitimately
# changes, delete the body below these comments, then regenerate it with:
#   diff -U0 docs/agentic-harness.md harness/core/.claude/skills/handoff-routing/agentic-harness.md \
#     | grep -E '^[-+]' | grep -vE '^(---|\+\+\+)' >> harness/handbook-delta.expected
# Any other divergence is content drift between the two copies — fix at the owner.
-This document is the reference for how the harness machinery works — the single home for its purpose, supporting disciplines, iteration shape, agent roles, and handoff contract. The README summarizes this for a first read and links here; this document carries the detail.
+This document is the self-contained reference for how the harness machinery works — its purpose, supporting disciplines, iteration shape, agent roles, and handoff contract.
